<%# The command palette — ":" from anywhere that is not a text box.

    It lives in the layout because every app has one: the Paperboy sidebar's
    search box only exists on Paperboy pages, and COA, Billing, DAM, P2M, Data
    Runner and Admin Tools each render a sidebar of their own. The palette is
    the one search that is always there, and the only one that can see the
    whole system rather than the app you happen to be standing in.

    `target: "_top"` is what makes a result actually go somewhere. Turbo sends
    a link's response back into the frame that holds it unless told otherwise,
    and no page in the app contains a frame by this name — so every result used
    to land on "Content missing" instead of the page it named.

    The frame is lazy, so the destinations and the form list — an ACL pass and
    a template query — are not built until the first ":" of a session. %>
<div data-controller="command-palette">
  <div class="pb-modal-backdrop pb-palette-backdrop" hidden
       data-command-palette-target="modal"
       data-action="click->command-palette#backdropClose
                    turbo:frame-load->command-palette#focusInput">
    <div class="pb-modal pb-modal--lg pb-palette-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
         aria-label="Search forms and commands">
      <%= turbo_frame_tag "command_palette", src: command_palette_path, loading: "lazy", target: "_top" do %>
        <p class="pb-modal__message">Loading…</p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
